# Recognitio packet discipline

The recognitio skill assembles the relevant changes out of a pull
request or a commit range into one verified review packet. It
makes no judgement about the code. Judgement belongs to the review
skill downstream, which keeps its own axes and its own reporting
rules.

A review starts only on a packet whose manifest reads verified. A
failed packet is a stop, never a smaller yes. When verification
fails, the review says what is missing in plain words.

Derives from the canonical skill at
`.agents/skills/recognitio/SKILL.md`, sections Purpose, The tier
model, and The boundary. This rule restates that guidance and
adds no new instruction source.
